1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From Voss Bygdebok:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mass var son 'e5t Torbj'f8rn Gauteson Dal til Hov i Fresvik, Sogn, som var av Dal'e6tti. Til Voss er Mass komen um lag 1660. Han tente fyrst hj'e5 presten Gjert Miltzow, vart so gift med enkja etter Johannes Sverkveson millom 'e5r
2 CONC i 1670 og 1686, og vart dermed buande p'e5 Seve. Han var f'f8dd um lag 1645, gift andre gongen 1703 med Ingebj'f8rg Larsdr. Uppheim, Vestb., tridje venda med Torbj'f8rg N. Midtun og d'f8ydde 1715. Mass var lensmann p'e5 Voss 1686-
2 CONC 1706. Som l'f8n fekk han 1696-1699 4 rd. 'e5rleg. 'c6ttingane reiste 1921 ein minnestein um Mass p'e5 Seve. Med henne Ingebj'f8rg hadde Mass seks born: Soffi f. 1705 (g. 1723 m. ekm. Steffa Nilsson Skjerve og 1736 m. Arnved Jonson
2 CONC  Vestrheim, Ulvik, som budde p'e5 Skjerve), Kristi f. 1705, (g. m. 1. Arve Arveson Rene, R'f8te, 2. m. Lars Person --- side 141 --- Vetla R'f8te), Brita f. 1708 (g. m. 1. Klas Knutson Finne, 2. med Isak Hermundson Gjerme), Margret
2 CONC a f. 1709 (g. m. 1. Anders Eirikson Lydvo, 2. m. Nils Nilsson Mug'e5s), Torbj'f8rn f. 1712, Gjertrud f. 1713, d'f8d 1716. 'c6tti har spreidt seg vidt utover p'e5 Voss. Mass fekk um lag 2 laup i Seve med fyrste kona si, kj'f8pte i 
2 CONC 1707 av Laurits Miltzow 2 laup 1 pund og 'e5tte d'e5 um lag 4 laup i Seve. Ved skifte etter andre kona 'e5t Mass 'e5tte dei dessutan 2 laup 2 pund i H'e6ve. Ho Torbj'f8rg, enkja etter Mass, vart attgift i 1717 med Knut Knutson Sei
2 CONC m og i 1721 med Mons Olavson Hornve. Dei budde og p'e5 Seve til dess Torbj'f8rn Masson tok mot garden, som han 'e5tte 4 laup i. Skreddar Berge Velomson hadde kj'f8pt 1 laup etter Adelus Bredahl og selde det 1723 til Jan von der Li
2 CONC ppe i Bergen. Sorenskrivar Fleischer kj'f8pte denne laupen 1753 og let han 1775 til Vangens Fatighus. Brita Johannesdr. sa i 1743 upp bygsli av ein part i garden og fekk d'e5 k'e5r hj'e5 Torbj'f8rn. Ho og mannen hennar m'e5 ho vor
2 CONC e leiglendingar p'e5 ein part i Seve. Torbj'f8rn Masson gifte seg 1733 med Gudve Knutsdr. Raustad, som var av Miltzow'e6tti. Han kj'f8pte 1761 l'f8ysningsretten til 4 laup i Seve og var brukar av heile garden. Han 'e5tte 'f2g 1 la
2 CONC up i Vestrheim og 3 spann i Hydningen, Vossastr. Torbj'f8rn og Gudve hadde ni born: Mass f. 1749, Gudleik f. 1752, Knut f. 1756, som vart buande p'e5 Vestrheim, Ingebj'f8rg f. 1737, g. m. Olav Sjurson Ronve, Kristense f. 1739, gif
2 CONC t til Kv'e5le, Gulfj. med Ivar Knutson, Gjertrud f. 1741, gift til Nest'e5s med Rognald Rognaldson, Guro f. 1747, gift til Sonve med Odd Nilsson, Anna f. 1743 og Ingjerd f. 1750, gift til Uppheim med Per Gusskalkson. Torbj'f8rn sk
2 CONC ifte sine 4 laup i Seve millom dei to eldste s'f8nene, Mass og Gudleik, bruk 1 og 3 Translated to English:
2 CONT
2 CONT S'e6ve Farm History
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1563, the name was written Seffuenn.  Below the farm is an underground spring (s'e6ve) where water runs through and gives the farm its name.  In 1777 the farm is taxed at 4 laup, 1 pund (pound), 6 mark (1 mark =1/4 kg).  During
2 CONC  the 1830s, taxation was comparable to 1800.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Winter feeding and crops (in acres) at S'e6ve:
2 CONT
2 CONT Horses Cattle  Goats and Sheep  Grain  Potatoes 1657 3 19  36    1723 2 29  36   40  1865 4 32  65   71 60 1918 7 24  56  
2 CONT
2 CONT 15 people lived at S'e6ve in 1801, 31 in 1865, and 25 in 1920.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mass was the son of Torbj'f8rn Gauteson Dal of Hov in Fresvik, Sogn, who was of Dal lineage.  Mass came to Voss in the 1660s.  He first worked for the priest Gjert Miltzow, and was married to the widow Johannes Sverkveson between 
2 CONC 1670 and 1686 and therefore became the farmer at S'e6ve.  He was born in 1645, married a second time in 1703 to Ingebj'f8rg Larsdatter Uppheim from Vestibygdi, and a third time to to Torbj'f8rg Nilsdatter Midtun.  He died in 1715.
2 CONC   Mass was the sheriff in Voss from 1686 to 1706.  For a salary between 1696 to 1699 he earned 4 riksdaler (1 riksdaler = 4 kroner) annually.  In 1921 his descendants erected a memorial stone of mass on S'e6ve.  With Ingebj'f8rg h
2 CONC e had six children.  The descendants have spread out all over Voss.  Mass got the territory with is first wife, purchased in 1707 from Klas Miltzow.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Torbj'f8rg, Masss widow, lived on the farm with her husbands until her stepson, Torbj'f8rn Masson took over.  Torbj'f8rn was married to Gudve Knutsdatter Raustad, who was a descendant of the Miltzow family.  In 1761 he bought S'e
2 CONC 6ve and became the owner of the entire farm.  Torbj'f8rn and Gudve had nine children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1764, Mass Torbj'f8rnson received part of S'e6ve from his father.  He married D'f8n'e5t Nilsdatter Sonve and had five children.  In 1769 Gudleik Torbj'f8rnson  received the other part of S'e6ve from his father.  He married Eli 
2 CONC Nilsdatter Gjelland in 1776 and had seven children.  The youngest daughter, Maria, married Brynjulv Hovde.  The two of them are our ancestors.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gudlieks oldest son, Torbj'f8rn, received half of his fathers share of the farm in 1807 and the remainder in 1822.  He married Ingjerd Vikingsdatter Gjerme and had six children.  Two of their sons, Viking and Nils, divided the f
2 CONC arm and each received one half.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Viking married Brita Torgeirsdatter Brekku and had six children.  One of their sons, Torbj'f8rn Gudliekson, bought the farm from his parents in 1880 for 2800 kroner.  Torbj'f8rs sold the farm in 1911 to Lars Person Skjelde for 500
2 CONC 0 kroner.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nils married Eli Oddsdatter H'e6ve in 1846.  They moved to America and sold their share of the farm to Ivar Andersson .  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mass Torbj'f8rnsons son, Knut Masson, received his inheritance in 1801.  He died unwed in 1837.  His sisters, Mari and Gudve, divided the estate between them.  Maris husband, Per, sold their half to their second son, Mass for 80
2 CONC 0 spd. in 1845.  Gudve and her husband, Arnfinn, sold their share to him in 1846.  Mass married the widow Rannveig Torbj'f8rnsdatter Leiddal in 1847.  They had no children and sold the farm to Mass Styrkson S'e6ve.  
