1 OCCU Sjøoffiser, godseier, Underfoud in Northmavine in 1589., Andrew (Anders) Lord of Hugoland Mowat, Godseier og Vice-Admiral, Skibssjef
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===ANDREW MOWAT OF HUGOLAND===
2 CONT
2 CONT =Wrong information=
2 CONT He could not have lived on Hovland, it was his son Axel who bought Hovland, Andrew was called of Hugoland (In Shetland!), Hugoland came to Andrew from his first wife Ursula.
2 CONT
2 CONT =About him=
2 CONT Andrew Mowat, of Assetter, of Hugoland (both in Northmavine, Shetland). Probably born around 1535. Underfoud in Northmavine in 1589 (or perhaps it was his son John).11 Died 1610/11.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1st before 25 September 1558 Ursula Tulloch, daughter of William Tulloch of Skea and probably Barbara Thomasdaughter. Ursula died before 1587.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 2nd shortly after 1587 Else Tronds, daughter of the Norwegian admiral Christoffer Trondsen and Karen Knutsdaughter Schanke. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After his second marriage he stayed in Norway in periods. The first years he stayed in Gjersvik (Tysnes, Norway), later at Hovland (also in Tysnes). But he always named himself "of Hugoland", even when he stayed in Norway. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Ursula Tulloch: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.John
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Malcolm
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Patrick
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Gilbert, ancestor of the Garth family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. James of Ure, of Burrafirth. Most likely born after 1577.Married Agnes Pitcairn, daughter of Mr James Pitcairn, minister of Northmaven.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son:
2 CONT
2 CONT a.  Gilbert, client of James Mowat in Paris. Married Margaret Forbes. He was a secretary to the Earl of Middleton and later to George, Marquis of Huntly from Whit 1662 to Whit 1663. Margaret died around 1714. She then lived in Can
2 CONC ongate.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Possibly: Barbara, married Edward Sinclair of Scalloway.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Possibly: Catherine, married John Neven of Scousburgh, and was probably mother to his son Ninian. She died after 1610.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by Else Tronds:
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.  Axel, of Hovland (in Tysnes, Norway).22 Born 1592. He was already in 1628 a captain in the Danish-Norwegian navy. In 1631 he became vice-admiral. Because of illness he had to leave the navy. The rest of his life he lived at Ho
2 CONC vland and became on of the greatest Norwegian landowners. His lands later was converted into the barony of Rosendal - the only Norwegian barony ever. He married around 1625 Karen Bildt, daughter of Knut Bildt of Morland and Lungeg
2 CONC ård and Sidsel Brun. Axel died 27. January 1661. His wife died 1662 in Bergen. They are buried in the burial chapel by the church in Rosendal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a. Axel. Naval officer. He was killed in a duel with his relative Lauritz Galtung of Torsnes in 1643.
2 CONT
2 CONT b.  Karen Mowat. Born around 1630. She married around 1658 Ludvig Rosenkrantz, later baron of Rosendal, and had issue, now extinct. Karen died in 1675 in Christiania (now Oslo).
2 CONT
2 CONT Natural son by Margrethe Eriksdaughter (daughter of Erik Jonsson of Brandvik and Susanne Pedersdaughter):
2 CONT
2 CONT c.  Anders Axelsen Helvik, ancestor of the Helvik-family.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Christoffer. Danish-Norwegian naval officer. He died 1628.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Karen.24 She married admiral Erik Orning of Vatne and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Natural child:
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.  Berald (Bartholomew)15, of Collafirth. Born around 1554. Probably the Berald Mowat in Blafirth (in Northmaven, Shetland) who was married to Marion Giffart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son:
2 CONT
2 CONT a. Malcolm, of Collafirth. Born around 1590. He may have been the father of
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) James, of Collafirth, father of
2 CONT
2 CONT a) Ursilla, married Laurence Tarrel of Voe, who died in 1715.
2 CONT
2 CONT  (http://cosoft.org/mowat/hugoland.html) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT After his second marriage he stayed in Norway in periods. The first years he stayed in Gjersvik (Tysnes, Norway), later at Hovland (also in Tysnes). But he always named himself "of Hugoland", even when he stayed in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders bodde med sin første kone i Skottland eller på Orknøyene. Siden kom han til Norge. Han skal ha vært Skipssjef. Han bodde med Else først på Store Gjersvik og senere på Hovland i Tysnes, Hordaland. Han eide også annet jordego
2 CONC ds, og var bl.a. med på kongehyllingen i Oslo i 1591.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Mowat of Hugoland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT kom til Norge fra Shetland eller Orknøyene.
2 CONT
2 CONT (NATURALIZATION: BEF 1558, Bosatte seg på Shetland. Nevnt blant den dansk-norske adel i 1591)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dette er det første vi hører om Mowat-slekten i Norge. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I følge slektsforskere som henviser til  'Dansk Adelskalender' skal denne "Mowalt"-slekten være av italiensk opprinnelse, fra en adel som bar navnet "Montealto", fordi den i latinsk brevutveksling fra middelalderen ble betegnet "d
2 CONC e Monte Alto"-slekten (???). 
2 CONT
2 CONT I følge mine undersøkelser synes imidlertid slekten å stamme fra Frankrike, fra stedet "Mont Haut" i Normandie, og at "Monte Alto" er en 'latinisering' av dette navnet (se nedenfor). Slekten kom derfra til de britiske øyer gjennom
2 CONC  medlemmer som fulgte Wilhelm Erobreren ('William the Conqueror') i 1066, der de slo seg ned i Mold i Flintshire, North Wales. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mold hette opprinnelig Mould, på walesisk Y Wyddgrug ('conspicuous barrow'). Den latinske oversettelsen av Mould er Mons altus, og derav den mest sannsynlige årsaken til at 'Mont Haut' ble ('latinisert') til 'Monte Alto' (!). Sted
2 CONC et er da også nedtegnet som "Mohald" i et dokument fra1254.....
2 CONT
2 CONT Derfra utbredde slekten seg hovedsaklig til Nord-Skottland, der den første nedtegnelsen av navnet synes å være Robert de Montealto, datert 1130, som var ansatt ved det kongelige hoff i Edinburgh under kong David I av Skottland (11
2 CONC 24 - 1139). Av kong William "the Lion" (1165-1214), sønnesønn av David I, ble de der tildelt grevskapet Fern i Forfarshire... 
2 CONT
2 CONT ...og derfra utbredte de seg igjen også til Irland, Orknøyene og Shetland - og så da til Norge med Anders Mowat i ca. 1550...
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT -------------------- https://groups.google.com/forum/?fromgroups=#!topic/soc.genealogy.medieval/HrAqAioYXwU
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Andrew kom i fra Shetland, han skreiv seg til Gården Haukeland. Hans tidligere kone Ursula Thomasdatter Thallag av Foblisetter som venetelig var i fra gården Foubister på Orkenøyenen. Andrew hadde barn i sitt førdte ekteskap. Det 
2 CONC synes som om farsslekt kom i fra Normandie til England på 1100 tallet(er noe usikkert).Andrew hadde vore ombodsmann for eit større adelsgods på Shetland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Orkenøyene http://www.ancestralorkney.com/index.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://vagshaug.no/allslekt/11439.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cosoft.org/mowat/hugoland.html
2 CONT
2 CONT This branch includes Mowats on Shetland and in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT I 	
2 CONT
2 CONT Bartholomew Mowat. Probably the ancestor of this family. He is not mentioned in any contemporary sources and therefore probably died young. There is no doubt that his son, Andrew, was a close relative to the Balquholly family, and
2 CONC  Bartholomew therefore probably was a younger son of Magnus of Balquholly. He married Barbara Sinclair, who neither is mentioned in any contemporary sources. But Andrew Mowat's coat of arms shows that his mother was probably a Sin
2 CONC clair.
