3 CTRY Norway
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} She was orphaned by the death of Marta Hansdatter Gjøen, who died in 1758, and lived with her maternal grandparents at Gjøn, Fusa, Hordaland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lisbeth Rasmusdatter was a very capable woman who "wore both the pants and the skirt of the household" which led to Knut Knutsson Tysse being called Lisbet'n around the parish. ('n is a masculine name suffix in the local dialect.)
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT She appeared on the 1801 Census at Tysse ytre, Samnanger, Hordaland, with her husband, children and a servant, as: Lisbeth Rasmusdatter, his wife (Hans kone), 55, both in their first marriage (Begge i første ægteskab).
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde: http://www.tuftin.net/genealogy/p7.htm#i683
